{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R3wYaDqzNzdZ4RpCHzD5KK","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t-- Procurement agent schema. Applied by the migration job with the\n     2\t-- procurement_owner role; the running agent connects as procurement_agent.\n     3\t\n     4\tCREATE TABLE audit_events (\n     5\t    node_id             text PRIMARY KEY,\n     6\t    parent_node_id      text REFERENCES audit_events (node_id),\n     7\t    run_id              text NOT NULL,\n     8\t    ts                  timestamptz NOT NULL,\n     9\t    kind                text NOT NULL,\n    10\t    accountable_party   text NOT NULL CHECK (accountable_party <> ''),\n    11\t    operational_owner   text NOT NULL CHECK (operational_owner <> ''),\n    12\t    tenant              text NOT NULL CHECK (tenant <> ''),\n    13\t    agent_type_id       text NOT NULL CHECK (agent_type_id <> ''),\n    14\t    agent_instance_id   text NOT NULL CHECK (agent_instance_id <> ''),\n    15\t    trace_id            text NOT NULL CHECK (trace_id <> ''),\n    16\t    span_id             text,\n    17\t    delegated_subject   text NOT NULL,\n    18\t    agent_principal     text NOT NULL,\n    19\t    parent_instance_id  text,\n    20\t    policy_version      text,\n    21\t    approval_id         text,\n    22\t    operation_id        text,\n    23\t    context_tokens      integer CHECK (context_tokens IS NULL OR context_tokens > 0),\n    24\t    context_method      text NOT NULL,\n    25\t    context_compacted   boolean NOT NULL,\n    26\t    payload             jsonb NOT NULL\n    27\t);\n    28\tCREATE INDEX audit_events_run ON audit_events (run_id, ts);\n    29\tCREATE INDEX audit_events_instance ON audit_events (agent_instance_id, ts);\n    30\tCREATE INDEX audit_events_trace ON audit_events (trace_id);\n    31\t\n    32\tCREATE TABLE approvals (\n    33\t    id                     text PRIMARY KEY,\n    34\t    tool                   text NOT NULL,\n    35\t    target                 text NOT NULL,\n    36\t    args_sha256            text NOT NULL,\n    37\t    args_summary           jsonb NOT NULL,\n    38\t    tenant                 text NOT NULL,\n    39\t    requested_by_instance  text NOT NULL,\n    40\t    requested_by_run       text NOT NULL,\n    41\t    delegated_subject      text NOT NULL,\n    42\t    status                 text NOT NULL CHECK (status IN ('pending', 'approved', 'rejected', 'expired')),\n    43\t    requested_at           timestamptz NOT NULL,\n    44\t    expires_at             timestamptz NOT NULL,\n    45\t    approver               text,\n    46\t    approver_role          text,\n    47\t    decided_at             timestamptz\n    48\t);\n    49\tCREATE INDEX approvals_lookup ON approvals (tool, target, tenant, status);\n    50\t\n    51\tCREATE TABLE approvers (\n    52\t    slack_user_id  text PRIMARY KEY,\n    53\t    email          text NOT NULL,\n    54\t    role           text NOT NULL,\n    55\t    business_unit  text NOT NULL,\n    56\t    active         boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT true\n    57\t);\n    58\t\n    59\tCREATE TABLE documents (\n    60\t    doc_id         text PRIMARY KEY,\n    61\t    business_unit  text NOT NULL,\n    62\t    source         text NOT NULL,\n    63\t    media_type     text NOT NULL,\n    64\t    sha256         text NOT NULL,\n    65\t    status         text NOT NULL CHECK (status IN ('accepted', 'quarantined')),\n    66\t    reject_reason  text,\n    67\t    text           text,\n    68\t    received_at    timestamptz NOT NULL\n    69\t);\n    70\tCREATE INDEX documents_bu ON documents (business_unit, doc_id);\n    71\t\n    72\tCREATE TABLE dept_notes (\n    73\t    note_id            text PRIMARY KEY,\n    74\t    business_unit      text NOT NULL,\n    75\t    department         text NOT NULL,\n    76\t    kind               text NOT NULL,\n    77\t    body               text NOT NULL,\n    78\t    verified           boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT false,\n    79\t    verified_by        text,\n    80\t    quarantined        boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT false,\n    81\t    expires_at         timestamptz,\n    82\t    writer_instance    text NOT NULL,\n    83\t    writer_type_id     text NOT NULL,\n    84\t    run_id             text NOT NULL,\n    85\t    source_doc_id      text,\n    86\t    delegated_subject  text NOT NULL,\n    87\t    context_tokens     integer,\n    88\t    context_method     text NOT NULL,\n    89\t    created_at         timestamptz NOT NULL\n    90\t);\n    91\tCREATE INDEX dept_notes_lookup ON dept_notes (business_unit, department, created_at DESC);\n    92\tCREATE INDEX dept_notes_source ON dept_notes (source_doc_id);\n    93\tCREATE INDEX dept_notes_writer ON dept_notes (writer_instance);\n    94\t\n    95\tCREATE TABLE control_flags (\n    96\t    scope    text PRIMARY KEY,           -- 'fleet' or 'tenant:<business_unit>'\n    97\t    halted   boolean NOT NULL,\n    98\t    reason   text NOT NULL,\n    99\t    set_by   text NOT NULL,\n   100\t    set_at   timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n   101\t);\n   102\t\n   103\tCREATE TABLE spend_quota (\n   104\t    scope      text NOT NULL,\n   105\t    key        text NOT NULL,\n   106\t    day        date NOT NULL,\n   107\t    spent_usd  numeric(12, 4) NOT NULL,\n   108\t    PRIMARY KEY (scope, key, day)\n   109\t);\n   110\t\n   111\tCREATE TABLE run_start_window (\n   112\t    scope   text NOT NULL,\n   113\t    key     text NOT NULL,\n   114\t    minute  timestamptz NOT NULL,\n   115\t    starts  integer NOT NULL,\n   116\t    PRIMARY KEY (scope, key, minute)\n   117\t);\n   118\t\n   119\t-- Runtime role: append-only audit, no access to control flags beyond reading.\n   120\tREVOKE ALL ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA public FROM procurement_agent;\n   121\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT ON audit_events TO procurement_agent;\n   122\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON approvals TO procurement_agent;\n   123\tGRANT SELECT ON approvers TO procurement_agent;\n   124\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT ON documents TO procurement_agent;\n   125\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT ON dept_notes TO procurement_agent;\n   126\tGRANT SELECT ON control_flags TO procurement_agent;\n   127\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON spend_quota TO procurement_agent;\n   128\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON run_start_window TO procurement_agent;\n   129\t\n   130\t-- Operators: halt and resume.\n   131\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON control_flags TO procurement_ops;\n   132\tGRANT SELECT ON audit_events TO procurement_ops;\n   133\tGRANT SELECT, UPDATE (verified, verified_by, quarantined) ON dept_notes TO procurement_ops;\n     1\tversion: \"proc-policy-2026.09.3\"\n     2\t\n     3\t# Operations that change money, vendor records, or purchase commitments.\n     4\t# Denied unless a valid approval exists for the operation and its target.\n     5\thigh_impact_tools:\n     6\t  - create_purchase_order\n     7\t  - pay_invoice\n     8\t\n     9\terp:\n    10\t  # Namespaces the agent may reach through the generic erp_call tool.\n    11\t  read_prefixes:\n    12\t    - \"budget.\"\n    13\t    - \"vendor.\"\n    14\t    - \"invoice.\"\n    15\t    - \"po.get\"\n    16\t    - \"po.list\"\n    17\t  # Scope requested from the STS for each ERP operation; the ERP enforces it.\n    18\t  operation_scopes:\n    19\t    budget.get_remaining: \"erp.read\"\n    20\t    vendor.get: \"erp.read\"\n    21\t    vendor.search: \"erp.read\"\n    22\t    vendor.update_remit_to: \"erp.read erp.vendor.write\"\n    23\t    invoice.get: \"erp.read\"\n    24\t    invoice.list_open: \"erp.read\"\n    25\t    invoice.mark_paid: \"erp.read erp.invoice.write\"\n    26\t    invoice.void: \"erp.read erp.invoice.write\"\n    27\t    po.get: \"erp.read\"\n    28\t    po.list_open: \"erp.read\"\n    29\t    po.create: \"erp.read erp.po.create\"\n    30\t\n    31\tapprovals:\n    32\t  ttl_minutes: 60\n    33\t  approver_roles:\n    34\t    pay_invoice: [ap_manager, finance_controller]\n    35\t    create_purchase_order: [budget_owner, finance_controller]\n    36\t    post_slack_message: [procurement_lead]\n    37\t\n    38\tbudgets:\n    39\t  per_run:\n    40\t    max_steps: 25\n    41\t    max_wall_seconds: 300\n    42\t    max_tokens: 400000\n    43\t    max_cost_usd: 4.00\n    44\t    max_tool_calls_per_minute: 30\n    45\t    max_subagents: 3\n    46\t  quotas_daily_usd:\n    47\t    user: 25\n    48\t    tenant: 250\n    49\t    fleet: 1500\n    50\t  run_starts_per_minute:\n    51\t    user: 5\n    52\t    tenant: 40\n    53\t    fleet: 200\n     1\t# Tools per agent role, each with the task reason it is granted.\n     2\troles:\n     3\t  procurement:\n     4\t    tools:\n     5\t      read_document: \"Read vendor quotes, invoices and emails that arrived through the mail gateway.\"\n     6\t      extract_line_items: \"Delegate line-item extraction from long documents to the extractor.\"\n     7\t      get_budget: \"Check remaining department budget before raising a purchase order.\"\n     8\t      erp_call: \"Look up vendors, open invoices and purchase orders for matching.\"\n     9\t      create_purchase_order: \"Raise a purchase order once a quote is within budget and approved.\"\n    10\t      pay_invoice: \"Pay an invoice that is matched to a purchase order and approved.\"\n    11\t      post_slack_message: \"Ask staff for missing details and confirm orders with vendors.\"\n    12\t      memory_read: \"Recall department preferences and contract terms from earlier runs.\"\n    13\t      memory_write: \"Save new department preferences and contract terms.\"\n    14\t  extractor:\n    15\t    tools:\n    16\t      read_document: \"Read the document whose line items are being extracted.\"\n     1\t\"\"\"Policy gate for tool calls.\n     2\t\n     3\tRuns in the harness between the model's proposed call and the integration.\n     4\tHigh-impact operations are denied unless a valid approval exists; when none\n     5\texists an approval request is opened and the call returns as pending.\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     8\t\n     9\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n    10\tfrom typing import Any\n    11\t\n    12\tfrom app.approvals import ApprovalStore\n    13\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n    14\t\n    15\t\n    16\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n    17\tclass Decision:\n    18\t    allow: bool\n    19\t    reason: str\n    20\t    policy_version: str\n    21\t    approval_id: str | None = None\n    22\t    pending: bool = False\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\tclass PolicyGate:\n    26\t    def __init__(self, policy: dict, approvals: ApprovalStore):\n    27\t        self.version: str = policy[\"version\"]\n    28\t        self.high_impact: frozenset[str] = frozenset(policy[\"high_impact_tools\"])\n    29\t        self.erp_read_prefixes: tuple[str, ...] = tuple(policy[\"erp\"][\"read_prefixes\"])\n    30\t        self.approvals = approvals\n    31\t\n    32\t    async def authorize(self, ident: RunIdentity, tool, args: dict[str, Any]) -> Decision:\n    33\t        if tool.name == \"erp_call\":\n    34\t            operation = str(args.get(\"operation\", \"\"))\n    35\t            if not operation.startswith(self.erp_read_prefixes):\n    36\t                return Decision(False, f\"erp operation not permitted: {operation}\", self.version)\n    37\t            return Decision(True, \"erp read operation\", self.version)\n    38\t\n    39\t        if tool.name == \"post_slack_message\":\n    40\t            if args.get(\"external\", False):\n    41\t                return await self._require_approval(ident, tool, args)\n    42\t            return Decision(True, \"internal staff message\", self.version)\n    43\t\n    44\t        if tool.name in self.high_impact:\n    45\t            return await self._require_approval(ident, tool, args)\n    46\t\n    47\t        return Decision(True, \"low-impact tool\", self.version)\n    48\t\n    49\t    async def _require_approval(self, ident: RunIdentity, tool, args: dict[str, Any]) -> Decision:\n    50\t        target = tool.target_of(args)\n    51\t        approval = await self.approvals.find_valid(ident, tool.name, target)\n    52\t        if approval is not None:\n    53\t            return Decision(True, \"approved\", self.version, approval_id=approval.id)\n    54\t        approval_id = await self.approvals.request(ident, tool.name, target, args)\n    55\t        return Decision(\n    56\t            False,\n    57\t            \"approval required; request opened\",\n    58\t            self.version,\n    59\t            approval_id=approval_id,\n    60\t            pending=True,\n    61\t        )\n     1\t\"\"\"Runtime settings, read once from the environment at process start.\"\"\"\n     2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     3\t\n     4\timport os\n     5\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n     6\tfrom functools import lru_cache\n     7\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     8\t\n     9\timport yaml\n    10\t\n    11\t\n    12\tdef _env(name: str, default: str | None = None) -> str:\n    13\t    value = os.environ.get(name, default)\n    14\t    if value is None:\n    15\t        raise RuntimeError(f\"missing required setting {name}\")\n    16\t    return value\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n    20\tclass Settings:\n    21\t    database_url: str\n    22\t    erp_mcp_url: str\n    23\t    payments_api_url: str\n    24\t    slack_api_url: str\n    25\t    sts_url: str\n    26\t    oidc_issuer: str\n    27\t    oidc_audience: str\n    28\t    oidc_jwks_url: str\n    29\t    workload_token_path: str\n    30\t    slack_signing_secret_path: str\n    31\t    mail_gateway_hmac_path: str\n    32\t    model_id: str\n    33\t    extractor_model_id: str\n    34\t    manifest_path: Path\n    35\t    prompt_dir: Path\n    36\t    policy_path: Path\n    37\t    tools_path: Path\n    38\t    operational_owner: str\n    39\t    image_digest: str\n    40\t\n    41\t    @property\n    42\t    def policy(self) -> dict:\n    43\t        return _load_yaml(self.policy_path)\n    44\t\n    45\t    @property\n    46\t    def manifest(self) -> dict:\n    47\t        return _load_yaml(self.manifest_path)\n    48\t\n    49\t    @property\n    50\t    def budgets(self) -> dict:\n    51\t        return self.policy[\"budgets\"]\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef _load_yaml(path: Path) -> dict:\n    55\t    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n    56\t        return yaml.safe_load(fh)\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\t@lru_cache(maxsize=1)\n    60\tdef get_settings() -> Settings:\n    61\t    root = Path(_env(\"APP_ROOT\", \"/app\"))\n    62\t    return Settings(\n    63\t        database_url=_env(\"DATABASE_URL\"),\n    64\t        erp_mcp_url=_env(\"ERP_MCP_URL\"),\n    65\t        payments_api_url=_env(\"PAYMENTS_API_URL\"),\n    66\t        slack_api_url=_env(\"SLACK_API_URL\", \"https://slack.com/api\"),\n    67\t        sts_url=_env(\"STS_URL\"),\n    68\t        oidc_issuer=_env(\"OIDC_ISSUER\"),\n    69\t        oidc_audience=_env(\"OIDC_AUDIENCE\", \"procurement-agent\"),\n    70\t        oidc_jwks_url=_env(\"OIDC_JWKS_URL\"),\n    71\t        workload_token_path=_env(\n    72\t            \"WORKLOAD_TOKEN_PATH\", \"/var/run/secrets/tokens/procurement-agent\"\n    73\t        ),\n    74\t        slack_signing_secret_path=_env(\n    75\t            \"SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET_PATH\", \"/var/run/secrets/slack/signing-secret\"\n    76\t        ),\n    77\t        mail_gateway_hmac_path=_env(\n    78\t            \"MAIL_GATEWAY_HMAC_PATH\", \"/var/run/secrets/mail/hmac-key\"\n    79\t        ),\n    80\t        model_id=_env(\"MODEL_ID\"),\n    81\t        extractor_model_id=_env(\"EXTRACTOR_MODEL_ID\"),\n    82\t        manifest_path=root / \"release\" / \"manifest.yaml\",\n    83\t        prompt_dir=root / \"prompts\",\n    84\t        policy_path=root / \"config\" / \"policy.yaml\",\n    85\t        tools_path=root / \"config\" / \"tools.yaml\",\n    86\t        operational_owner=_env(\"OPERATIONAL_OWNER\", \"team-procurement-platform\"),\n    87\t        image_digest=_env(\"IMAGE_DIGEST\"),\n    88\t    )\n     1\t\"\"\"Startup checks: compare the running artifacts with the release manifest.\"\"\"\n     2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     3\t\n     4\timport hashlib\n     5\timport logging\n     6\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     7\t\n     8\tfrom app.identity import compute_agent_type_id\n     9\tfrom app.settings import Settings\n    10\t\n    11\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    12\t\n    13\t\n    14\tdef sha256_file(path: Path) -> str:\n    15\t    return \"sha256:\" + hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n    16\t\n    17\t\n    18\tdef running_state_mismatches(settings: Settings, manifest: dict) -> list[str]:\n    19\t    mismatches: list[str] = []\n    20\t    if settings.image_digest != manifest[\"image\"][\"digest\"]:\n    21\t        mismatches.append(f\"image: running {settings.image_digest}\")\n    22\t    for name, entry in manifest[\"prompts\"].items():\n    23\t        path = settings.prompt_dir / Path(entry[\"path\"]).name\n    24\t        if not path.exists() or sha256_file(path) != entry[\"sha256\"]:\n    25\t            mismatches.append(f\"prompt:{name}\")\n    26\t    for name in (\"policy\", \"tools\"):\n    27\t        entry = manifest[\"config\"][name]\n    28\t        path = settings.policy_path if name == \"policy\" else settings.tools_path\n    29\t        if sha256_file(path) != entry[\"sha256\"]:\n    30\t            mismatches.append(f\"config:{name}\")\n    31\t    if settings.model_id != manifest[\"models\"][\"primary\"][\"model_id\"]:\n    32\t        mismatches.append(\"model:primary\")\n    33\t    if settings.extractor_model_id != manifest[\"models\"][\"extractor\"][\"model_id\"]:\n    34\t        mismatches.append(\"model:extractor\")\n    35\t    return mismatches\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\tdef startup_checks(settings: Settings) -> str:\n    39\t    \"\"\"Return the agent-type-id for this process.\"\"\"\n    40\t    manifest = settings.manifest\n    41\t    mismatches = running_state_mismatches(settings, manifest)\n    42\t    if mismatches:\n    43\t        log.error(\"running state differs from release manifest: %s\", \", \".join(mismatches))\n    44\t    agent_type_id = compute_agent_type_id(manifest)\n    45\t    log.info(\"agent_type_id=%s release=%s\", agent_type_id, manifest[\"release\"])\n    46\t    return agent_type_id\n     1\t\"\"\"Decision-time context size.\n     2\t\n     3\tCounting method (documented in README, \"Context size\"):\n     4\t\n     5\t1. Before each model call, the exact request (system prompt, messages and\n     6\t   tool schemas) is sent to the provider's token-counting endpoint. The\n     7\t   returned ``input_tokens`` is recorded with method ``count_tokens_api``.\n     8\t   This is the size of the context the model decides on, including any\n     9\t   prefix that will be served from the prompt cache.\n    10\t2. If counting fails, the value is taken after the call from the response\n    11\t   usage as ``input_tokens + cache_read_input_tokens +\n    12\t   cache_creation_input_tokens`` and recorded with method\n    13\t   ``usage_sum_estimate``.\n    14\t3. If neither is available the value is ``NULL`` with method\n    15\t   ``unavailable``. It is never recorded as zero.\n    16\t\n    17\t``compacted`` is true when the harness dropped or summarized earlier turns\n    18\tbefore this call. Provider-side truncation is not visible to the harness and\n    19\tis listed as a known limit.\n    20\t\"\"\"\n    21\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n    22\t\n    23\timport logging\n    24\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, replace\n    25\t\n    26\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n    30\tclass ContextMeasure:\n    31\t    tokens: int | None\n    32\t    method: str\n    33\t    compacted: bool\n    34\t\n    35\t    @classmethod\n    36\t    def unavailable(cls, compacted: bool = False) -> \"ContextMeasure\":\n    37\t        return cls(tokens=None, method=\"unavailable\", compacted=compacted)\n    38\t\n    39\t    def finalize(self, usage) -> \"ContextMeasure\":\n    40\t        if self.tokens is not None:\n    41\t            return self\n    42\t        if usage is None:\n    43\t            return ContextMeasure.unavailable(self.compacted)\n    44\t        total = (\n    45\t            int(usage.input_tokens or 0)\n    46\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_read_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n    47\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n    48\t        )\n    49\t        if total <= 0:\n    50\t            return ContextMeasure.unavailable(self.compacted)\n    51\t        return replace(self, tokens=total, method=\"usage_sum_estimate\")\n    52\t\n    53\t    def otel_attributes(self) -> dict:\n    54\t        attrs = {\n    55\t            \"procurement.context.method\": self.method,\n    56\t            \"gen_ai.conversation.compacted\": self.compacted,\n    57\t        }\n    58\t        if self.tokens is not None:\n    59\t            attrs[\"procurement.context.tokens\"] = self.tokens\n    60\t        return attrs\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tasync def measure_context(client, request: dict, compacted: bool) -> ContextMeasure:\n    64\t    try:\n    65\t        counted = await client.messages.count_tokens(\n    66\t            model=request[\"model\"],\n    67\t            system=request[\"system\"],\n    68\t            messages=request[\"messages\"],\n    69\t            tools=request[\"tools\"],\n    70\t        )\n    71\t        return ContextMeasure(int(counted.input_tokens), \"count_tokens_api\", compacted)\n    72\t    except Exception:  # counting is best effort; finalize() falls back to usage\n    73\t        log.warning(\"token count failed; falling back to usage\", exc_info=True)\n    74\t        return ContextMeasure(tokens=None, method=\"pending_usage\", compacted=compacted)\n     1\t# procurement-agent\n     2\t\n     3\tProcurement agent for Example Corp business units. It reads vendor quotes and\n     4\tinvoices that arrive by email, checks them against department budgets, raises\n     5\tpurchase orders in the ERP, pays matched invoices, and talks to staff and\n     6\tvendors in Slack. It keeps short per-department notes between runs.\n     7\t\n     8\t## Architecture\n     9\t\n    10\t```\n    11\tmail gateway --HMAC--> /ingest/mail --> documents (Postgres, per business unit)\n    12\tstaff (OIDC JWT) ----> /runs --> ProcurementAgent loop (app/loop.py)\n    13\t                                   |-- PolicyGate (app/gate.py) + approvals (Slack buttons)\n    14\t                                   |-- Budget (app/budget.py)\n    15\t                                   |-- audit graph (app/audit.py -> audit_events)\n    16\t                                   |-- tools:\n    17\t                                   |     read_document, extract_line_items -> LineItemExtractor sub-agent\n    18\t                                   |     get_budget, erp_call, create_purchase_order -> ERP MCP via gateway\n    19\t                                   |     pay_invoice -> payments API\n    20\t                                   |     post_slack_message -> Slack (via slack-proxy)\n    21\t                                   |     memory_read, memory_write -> dept_notes\n    22\t```\n    23\t\n    24\t* **Tenancy.** Each run belongs to one business unit, taken from the `bu`\n    25\t  claim of the caller's verified OIDC token. Documents, notes, approvals and\n    26\t  quotas are keyed by business unit.\n    27\t* **Identity.** The agent runs as the `procurement-agent` service account.\n    28\t  Its projected token (10-minute lifetime) is exchanged at the internal STS\n    29\t  for audience-bound tokens for the ERP gateway, payments API and Slack\n    30\t  proxy. User tokens are never forwarded.\n    31\t* **Approvals.** `create_purchase_order`, `pay_invoice` and vendor messages\n    32\t  require an approval from a role listed in `config/policy.yaml`. Approval\n    33\t  requests are posted to `#approvals-<bu>` with the argument summary.\n    34\t* **Budgets.** Per-run step, time, token, cost, tool-rate and sub-agent\n    35\t  limits, plus per-user, per-business-unit and fleet quotas for daily spend\n    36\t  and run starts. See `config/policy.yaml`.\n    37\t* **Audit.** Every run step is a row in `audit_events` linked to its parent\n    38\t  step, with the six identity fields, policy version, approval id and\n    39\t  decision-time context size. The agent's database role can insert audit\n    40\t  rows but not update or delete them.\n    41\t\n    42\t## Context size\n    43\t\n    44\tLogged on every audit row as `context_tokens` and `context_method`:\n    45\t\n    46\t| method | meaning |\n    47\t|---|---|\n    48\t| `count_tokens_api` | exact request counted with the provider's token-count endpoint before the call (includes cached prefix) |\n    49\t| `usage_sum_estimate` | counting failed; `input_tokens + cache_read + cache_creation` from the response |\n    50\t| `unavailable` | neither available; `context_tokens` is NULL, never 0 |\n    51\t\n    52\t`context_compacted` is true when the harness dropped earlier turns before the\n    53\tcall (`app/loop.py:_compact`). Provider-side truncation is not visible.\n    54\t\n    55\t## Operating\n    56\t\n    57\t* **Halt.** Insert or update a row in `control_flags` (`scope = 'fleet'` or\n    58\t  `'tenant:<bu>'`, `halted = true`) as `procurement_ops`. New runs refuse to\n    59\t  start while a halt is set.\n    60\t* **Release.** Merges to `main` build, sign (keyless cosign), and attest the\n    61\t  image (SLSA provenance and CycloneDX SBOM). Kyverno rejects unsigned or\n    62\t  unattested images in `procurement-prod`.\n    63\t* **Network.** Default-deny egress with explicit rules for DNS, the egress\n    64\t  proxy, the Slack proxy, the database, the ERP gateway and the STS.\n    65\t\n    66\t## Tests\n    67\t\n    68\t```bash\n    69\tpip install -e '.[test]'\n    70\tpytest -q\n    71\t```\n.\n..\nci.yaml","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a55d5680-c612-41b9-ac94-a9988346fb54","uuid":"65f6ddbc-c25f-4628-bd2a-a75072695c0c","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:40:28.632Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     1\t-- Procurement agent schema. Applied by the migration job with the\n     2\t-- procurement_owner role; the running agent connects as procurement_agent.\n     3\t\n     4\tCREATE TABLE audit_events (\n     5\t    node_id             text PRIMARY KEY,\n     6\t    parent_node_id      text REFERENCES audit_events (node_id),\n     7\t    run_id              text NOT NULL,\n     8\t    ts                  timestamptz NOT NULL,\n     9\t    kind                text NOT NULL,\n    10\t    accountable_party   text NOT NULL CHECK (accountable_party <> ''),\n    11\t    operational_owner   text NOT NULL CHECK (operational_owner <> ''),\n    12\t    tenant              text NOT NULL CHECK (tenant <> ''),\n    13\t    agent_type_id       text NOT NULL CHECK (agent_type_id <> ''),\n    14\t    agent_instance_id   text NOT NULL CHECK (agent_instance_id <> ''),\n    15\t    trace_id            text NOT NULL CHECK (trace_id <> ''),\n    16\t    span_id             text,\n    17\t    delegated_subject   text NOT NULL,\n    18\t    agent_principal     text NOT NULL,\n    19\t    parent_instance_id  text,\n    20\t    policy_version      text,\n    21\t    approval_id         text,\n    22\t    operation_id        text,\n    23\t    context_tokens      integer CHECK (context_tokens IS NULL OR context_tokens > 0),\n    24\t    context_method      text NOT NULL,\n    25\t    context_compacted   boolean NOT NULL,\n    26\t    payload             jsonb NOT NULL\n    27\t);\n    28\tCREATE INDEX audit_events_run ON audit_events (run_id, ts);\n    29\tCREATE INDEX audit_events_instance ON audit_events (agent_instance_id, ts);\n    30\tCREATE INDEX audit_events_trace ON audit_events (trace_id);\n    31\t\n    32\tCREATE TABLE approvals (\n    33\t    id                     text PRIMARY KEY,\n    34\t    tool                   text NOT NULL,\n    35\t    target                 text NOT NULL,\n    36\t    args_sha256            text NOT NULL,\n    37\t    args_summary           jsonb NOT NULL,\n    38\t    tenant                 text NOT NULL,\n    39\t    requested_by_instance  text NOT NULL,\n    40\t    requested_by_run       text NOT NULL,\n    41\t    delegated_subject      text NOT NULL,\n    42\t    status                 text NOT NULL CHECK (status IN ('pending', 'approved', 'rejected', 'expired')),\n    43\t    requested_at           timestamptz NOT NULL,\n    44\t    expires_at             timestamptz NOT NULL,\n    45\t    approver               text,\n    46\t    approver_role          text,\n    47\t    decided_at             timestamptz\n    48\t);\n    49\tCREATE INDEX approvals_lookup ON approvals (tool, target, tenant, status);\n    50\t\n    51\tCREATE TABLE approvers (\n    52\t    slack_user_id  text PRIMARY KEY,\n    53\t    email          text NOT NULL,\n    54\t    role           text NOT NULL,\n    55\t    business_unit  text NOT NULL,\n    56\t    active         boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT true\n    57\t);\n    58\t\n    59\tCREATE TABLE documents (\n    60\t    doc_id         text PRIMARY KEY,\n    61\t    business_unit  text NOT NULL,\n    62\t    source         text NOT NULL,\n    63\t    media_type     text NOT NULL,\n    64\t    sha256         text NOT NULL,\n    65\t    status         text NOT NULL CHECK (status IN ('accepted', 'quarantined')),\n    66\t    reject_reason  text,\n    67\t    text           text,\n    68\t    received_at    timestamptz NOT NULL\n    69\t);\n    70\tCREATE INDEX documents_bu ON documents (business_unit, doc_id);\n    71\t\n    72\tCREATE TABLE dept_notes (\n    73\t    note_id            text PRIMARY KEY,\n    74\t    business_unit      text NOT NULL,\n    75\t    department         text NOT NULL,\n    76\t    kind               text NOT NULL,\n    77\t    body               text NOT NULL,\n    78\t    verified           boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT false,\n    79\t    verified_by        text,\n    80\t    quarantined        boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT false,\n    81\t    expires_at         timestamptz,\n    82\t    writer_instance    text NOT NULL,\n    83\t    writer_type_id     text NOT NULL,\n    84\t    run_id             text NOT NULL,\n    85\t    source_doc_id      text,\n    86\t    delegated_subject  text NOT NULL,\n    87\t    context_tokens     integer,\n    88\t    context_method     text NOT NULL,\n    89\t    created_at         timestamptz NOT NULL\n    90\t);\n    91\tCREATE INDEX dept_notes_lookup ON dept_notes (business_unit, department, created_at DESC);\n    92\tCREATE INDEX dept_notes_source ON dept_notes (source_doc_id);\n    93\tCREATE INDEX dept_notes_writer ON dept_notes (writer_instance);\n    94\t\n    95\tCREATE TABLE control_flags (\n    96\t    scope    text PRIMARY KEY,           -- 'fleet' or 'tenant:<business_unit>'\n    97\t    halted   boolean NOT NULL,\n    98\t    reason   text NOT NULL,\n    99\t    set_by   text NOT NULL,\n   100\t    set_at   timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n   101\t);\n   102\t\n   103\tCREATE TABLE spend_quota (\n   104\t    scope      text NOT NULL,\n   105\t    key        text NOT NULL,\n   106\t    day        date NOT NULL,\n   107\t    spent_usd  numeric(12, 4) NOT NULL,\n   108\t    PRIMARY KEY (scope, key, day)\n   109\t);\n   110\t\n   111\tCREATE TABLE run_start_window (\n   112\t    scope   text NOT NULL,\n   113\t    key     text NOT NULL,\n   114\t    minute  timestamptz NOT NULL,\n   115\t    starts  integer NOT NULL,\n   116\t    PRIMARY KEY (scope, key, minute)\n   117\t);\n   118\t\n   119\t-- Runtime role: append-only audit, no access to control flags beyond reading.\n   120\tREVOKE ALL ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA public FROM procurement_agent;\n   121\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT ON audit_events TO procurement_agent;\n   122\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON approvals TO procurement_agent;\n   123\tGRANT SELECT ON approvers TO procurement_agent;\n   124\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT ON documents TO procurement_agent;\n   125\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT ON dept_notes TO procurement_agent;\n   126\tGRANT SELECT ON control_flags TO procurement_agent;\n   127\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON spend_quota TO procurement_agent;\n   128\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON run_start_window TO procurement_agent;\n   129\t\n   130\t-- Operators: halt and resume.\n   131\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON control_flags TO procurement_ops;\n   132\tGRANT SELECT ON audit_events TO procurement_ops;\n   133\tGRANT SELECT, UPDATE (verified, verified_by, quarantined) ON dept_notes TO procurement_ops;\n     1\tversion: \"proc-policy-2026.09.3\"\n     2\t\n     3\t# Operations that change money, vendor records, or purchase commitments.\n     4\t# Denied unless a valid approval exists for the operation and its target.\n     5\thigh_impact_tools:\n     6\t  - create_purchase_order\n     7\t  - pay_invoice\n     8\t\n     9\terp:\n    10\t  # Namespaces the agent may reach through the generic erp_call tool.\n    11\t  read_prefixes:\n    12\t    - \"budget.\"\n    13\t    - \"vendor.\"\n    14\t    - \"invoice.\"\n    15\t    - \"po.get\"\n    16\t    - \"po.list\"\n    17\t  # Scope requested from the STS for each ERP operation; the ERP enforces it.\n    18\t  operation_scopes:\n    19\t    budget.get_remaining: \"erp.read\"\n    20\t    vendor.get: \"erp.read\"\n    21\t    vendor.search: \"erp.read\"\n    22\t    vendor.update_remit_to: \"erp.read erp.vendor.write\"\n    23\t    invoice.get: \"erp.read\"\n    24\t    invoice.list_open: \"erp.read\"\n    25\t    invoice.mark_paid: \"erp.read erp.invoice.write\"\n    26\t    invoice.void: \"erp.read erp.invoice.write\"\n    27\t    po.get: \"erp.read\"\n    28\t    po.list_open: \"erp.read\"\n    29\t    po.create: \"erp.read erp.po.create\"\n    30\t\n    31\tapprovals:\n    32\t  ttl_minutes: 60\n    33\t  approver_roles:\n    34\t    pay_invoice: [ap_manager, finance_controller]\n    35\t    create_purchase_order: [budget_owner, finance_controller]\n    36\t    post_slack_message: [procurement_lead]\n    37\t\n    38\tbudgets:\n    39\t  per_run:\n    40\t    max_steps: 25\n    41\t    max_wall_seconds: 300\n    42\t    max_tokens: 400000\n    43\t    max_cost_usd: 4.00\n    44\t    max_tool_calls_per_minute: 30\n    45\t    max_subagents: 3\n    46\t  quotas_daily_usd:\n    47\t    user: 25\n    48\t    tenant: 250\n    49\t    fleet: 1500\n    50\t  run_starts_per_minute:\n    51\t    user: 5\n    52\t    tenant: 40\n    53\t    fleet: 200\n     1\t# Tools per agent role, each with the task reason it is granted.\n     2\troles:\n     3\t  procurement:\n     4\t    tools:\n     5\t      read_document: \"Read vendor quotes, invoices and emails that arrived through the mail gateway.\"\n     6\t      extract_line_items: \"Delegate line-item extraction from long documents to the extractor.\"\n     7\t      get_budget: \"Check remaining department budget before raising a purchase order.\"\n     8\t      erp_call: \"Look up vendors, open invoices and purchase orders for matching.\"\n     9\t      create_purchase_order: \"Raise a purchase order once a quote is within budget and approved.\"\n    10\t      pay_invoice: \"Pay an invoice that is matched to a purchase order and approved.\"\n    11\t      post_slack_message: \"Ask staff for missing details and confirm orders with vendors.\"\n    12\t      memory_read: \"Recall department preferences and contract terms from earlier runs.\"\n    13\t      memory_write: \"Save new department preferences and contract terms.\"\n    14\t  extractor:\n    15\t    tools:\n    16\t      read_document: \"Read the document whose line items are being extracted.\"\n     1\t\"\"\"Policy gate for tool calls.\n     2\t\n     3\tRuns in the harness between the model's proposed call and the integration.\n     4\tHigh-impact operations are denied unless a valid approval exists; when none\n     5\texists an approval request is opened and the call returns as pending.\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     8\t\n     9\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n    10\tfrom typing import Any\n    11\t\n    12\tfrom app.approvals import ApprovalStore\n    13\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n    14\t\n    15\t\n    16\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n    17\tclass Decision:\n    18\t    allow: bool\n    19\t    reason: str\n    20\t    policy_version: str\n    21\t    approval_id: str | None = None\n    22\t    pending: bool = False\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\tclass PolicyGate:\n    26\t    def __init__(self, policy: dict, approvals: ApprovalStore):\n    27\t        self.version: str = policy[\"version\"]\n    28\t        self.high_impact: frozenset[str] = frozenset(policy[\"high_impact_tools\"])\n    29\t        self.erp_read_prefixes: tuple[str, ...] = tuple(policy[\"erp\"][\"read_prefixes\"])\n    30\t        self.approvals = approvals\n    31\t\n    32\t    async def authorize(self, ident: RunIdentity, tool, args: dict[str, Any]) -> Decision:\n    33\t        if tool.name == \"erp_call\":\n    34\t            operation = str(args.get(\"operation\", \"\"))\n    35\t            if not operation.startswith(self.erp_read_prefixes):\n    36\t                return Decision(False, f\"erp operation not permitted: {operation}\", self.version)\n    37\t            return Decision(True, \"erp read operation\", self.version)\n    38\t\n    39\t        if tool.name == \"post_slack_message\":\n    40\t            if args.get(\"external\", False):\n    41\t                return await self._require_approval(ident, tool, args)\n    42\t            return Decision(True, \"internal staff message\", self.version)\n    43\t\n    44\t        if tool.name in self.high_impact:\n    45\t            return await self._require_approval(ident, tool, args)\n    46\t\n    47\t        return Decision(True, \"low-impact tool\", self.version)\n    48\t\n    49\t    async def _require_approval(self, ident: RunIdentity, tool, args: dict[str, Any]) -> Decision:\n    50\t        target = tool.target_of(args)\n    51\t        approval = await self.approvals.find_valid(ident, tool.name, target)\n    52\t        if approval is not None:\n    53\t            return Decision(True, \"approved\", self.version, approval_id=approval.id)\n    54\t        approval_id = await self.approvals.request(ident, tool.name, target, args)\n    55\t        return Decision(\n    56\t            False,\n    57\t            \"approval required; request opened\",\n    58\t            self.version,\n    59\t            approval_id=approval_id,\n    60\t            pending=True,\n    61\t        )\n     1\t\"\"\"Runtime settings, read once from the environment at process start.\"\"\"\n     2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     3\t\n     4\timport os\n     5\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n     6\tfrom functools import lru_cache\n     7\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     8\t\n     9\timport yaml\n    10\t\n    11\t\n    12\tdef _env(name: str, default: str | None = None) -> str:\n    13\t    value = os.environ.get(name, default)\n    14\t    if value is None:\n    15\t        raise RuntimeError(f\"missing required setting {name}\")\n    16\t    return value\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n    20\tclass Settings:\n    21\t    database_url: str\n    22\t    erp_mcp_url: str\n    23\t    payments_api_url: str\n    24\t    slack_api_url: str\n    25\t    sts_url: str\n    26\t    oidc_issuer: str\n    27\t    oidc_audience: str\n    28\t    oidc_jwks_url: str\n    29\t    workload_token_path: str\n    30\t    slack_signing_secret_path: str\n    31\t    mail_gateway_hmac_path: str\n    32\t    model_id: str\n    33\t    extractor_model_id: str\n    34\t    manifest_path: Path\n    35\t    prompt_dir: Path\n    36\t    policy_path: Path\n    37\t    tools_path: Path\n    38\t    operational_owner: str\n    39\t    image_digest: str\n    40\t\n    41\t    @property\n    42\t    def policy(self) -> dict:\n    43\t        return _load_yaml(self.policy_path)\n    44\t\n    45\t    @property\n    46\t    def manifest(self) -> dict:\n    47\t        return _load_yaml(self.manifest_path)\n    48\t\n    49\t    @property\n    50\t    def budgets(self) -> dict:\n    51\t        return self.policy[\"budgets\"]\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef _load_yaml(path: Path) -> dict:\n    55\t    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n    56\t        return yaml.safe_load(fh)\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\t@lru_cache(maxsize=1)\n    60\tdef get_settings() -> Settings:\n    61\t    root = Path(_env(\"APP_ROOT\", \"/app\"))\n    62\t    return Settings(\n    63\t        database_url=_env(\"DATABASE_URL\"),\n    64\t        erp_mcp_url=_env(\"ERP_MCP_URL\"),\n    65\t        payments_api_url=_env(\"PAYMENTS_API_URL\"),\n    66\t        slack_api_url=_env(\"SLACK_API_URL\", \"https://slack.com/api\"),\n    67\t        sts_url=_env(\"STS_URL\"),\n    68\t        oidc_issuer=_env(\"OIDC_ISSUER\"),\n    69\t        oidc_audience=_env(\"OIDC_AUDIENCE\", \"procurement-agent\"),\n    70\t        oidc_jwks_url=_env(\"OIDC_JWKS_URL\"),\n    71\t        workload_token_path=_env(\n    72\t            \"WORKLOAD_TOKEN_PATH\", \"/var/run/secrets/tokens/procurement-agent\"\n    73\t        ),\n    74\t        slack_signing_secret_path=_env(\n    75\t            \"SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET_PATH\", \"/var/run/secrets/slack/signing-secret\"\n    76\t        ),\n    77\t        mail_gateway_hmac_path=_env(\n    78\t            \"MAIL_GATEWAY_HMAC_PATH\", \"/var/run/secrets/mail/hmac-key\"\n    79\t        ),\n    80\t        model_id=_env(\"MODEL_ID\"),\n    81\t        extractor_model_id=_env(\"EXTRACTOR_MODEL_ID\"),\n    82\t        manifest_path=root / \"release\" / \"manifest.yaml\",\n    83\t        prompt_dir=root / \"prompts\",\n    84\t        policy_path=root / \"config\" / \"policy.yaml\",\n    85\t        tools_path=root / \"config\" / \"tools.yaml\",\n    86\t        operational_owner=_env(\"OPERATIONAL_OWNER\", \"team-procurement-platform\"),\n    87\t        image_digest=_env(\"IMAGE_DIGEST\"),\n    88\t    )\n     1\t\"\"\"Startup checks: compare the running artifacts with the release manifest.\"\"\"\n     2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     3\t\n     4\timport hashlib\n     5\timport logging\n     6\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     7\t\n     8\tfrom app.identity import compute_agent_type_id\n     9\tfrom app.settings import Settings\n    10\t\n    11\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    12\t\n    13\t\n    14\tdef sha256_file(path: Path) -> str:\n    15\t    return \"sha256:\" + hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n    16\t\n    17\t\n    18\tdef running_state_mismatches(settings: Settings, manifest: dict) -> list[str]:\n    19\t    mismatches: list[str] = []\n    20\t    if settings.image_digest != manifest[\"image\"][\"digest\"]:\n    21\t        mismatches.append(f\"image: running {settings.image_digest}\")\n    22\t    for name, entry in manifest[\"prompts\"].items():\n    23\t        path = settings.prompt_dir / Path(entry[\"path\"]).name\n    24\t        if not path.exists() or sha256_file(path) != entry[\"sha256\"]:\n    25\t            mismatches.append(f\"prompt:{name}\")\n    26\t    for name in (\"policy\", \"tools\"):\n    27\t        entry = manifest[\"config\"][name]\n    28\t        path = settings.policy_path if name == \"policy\" else settings.tools_path\n    29\t        if sha256_file(path) != entry[\"sha256\"]:\n    30\t            mismatches.append(f\"config:{name}\")\n    31\t    if settings.model_id != manifest[\"models\"][\"primary\"][\"model_id\"]:\n    32\t        mismatches.append(\"model:primary\")\n    33\t    if settings.extractor_model_id != manifest[\"models\"][\"extractor\"][\"model_id\"]:\n    34\t        mismatches.append(\"model:extractor\")\n    35\t    return mismatches\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\tdef startup_checks(settings: Settings) -> str:\n    39\t    \"\"\"Return the agent-type-id for this process.\"\"\"\n    40\t    manifest = settings.manifest\n    41\t    mismatches = running_state_mismatches(settings, manifest)\n    42\t    if mismatches:\n    43\t        log.error(\"running state differs from release manifest: %s\", \", \".join(mismatches))\n    44\t    agent_type_id = compute_agent_type_id(manifest)\n    45\t    log.info(\"agent_type_id=%s release=%s\", agent_type_id, manifest[\"release\"])\n    46\t    return agent_type_id\n     1\t\"\"\"Decision-time context size.\n     2\t\n     3\tCounting method (documented in README, \"Context size\"):\n     4\t\n     5\t1. Before each model call, the exact request (system prompt, messages and\n     6\t   tool schemas) is sent to the provider's token-counting endpoint. The\n     7\t   returned ``input_tokens`` is recorded with method ``count_tokens_api``.\n     8\t   This is the size of the context the model decides on, including any\n     9\t   prefix that will be served from the prompt cache.\n    10\t2. If counting fails, the value is taken after the call from the response\n    11\t   usage as ``input_tokens + cache_read_input_tokens +\n    12\t   cache_creation_input_tokens`` and recorded with method\n    13\t   ``usage_sum_estimate``.\n    14\t3. If neither is available the value is ``NULL`` with method\n    15\t   ``unavailable``. It is never recorded as zero.\n    16\t\n    17\t``compacted`` is true when the harness dropped or summarized earlier turns\n    18\tbefore this call. Provider-side truncation is not visible to the harness and\n    19\tis listed as a known limit.\n    20\t\"\"\"\n    21\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n    22\t\n    23\timport logging\n    24\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, replace\n    25\t\n    26\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n    30\tclass ContextMeasure:\n    31\t    tokens: int | None\n    32\t    method: str\n    33\t    compacted: bool\n    34\t\n    35\t    @classmethod\n    36\t    def unavailable(cls, compacted: bool = False) -> \"ContextMeasure\":\n    37\t        return cls(tokens=None, method=\"unavailable\", compacted=compacted)\n    38\t\n    39\t    def finalize(self, usage) -> \"ContextMeasure\":\n    40\t        if self.tokens is not None:\n    41\t            return self\n    42\t        if usage is None:\n    43\t            return ContextMeasure.unavailable(self.compacted)\n    44\t        total = (\n    45\t            int(usage.input_tokens or 0)\n    46\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_read_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n    47\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n    48\t        )\n    49\t        if total <= 0:\n    50\t            return ContextMeasure.unavailable(self.compacted)\n    51\t        return replace(self, tokens=total, method=\"usage_sum_estimate\")\n    52\t\n    53\t    def otel_attributes(self) -> dict:\n    54\t        attrs = {\n    55\t            \"procurement.context.method\": self.method,\n    56\t            \"gen_ai.conversation.compacted\": self.compacted,\n    57\t        }\n    58\t        if self.tokens is not None:\n    59\t            attrs[\"procurement.context.tokens\"] = self.tokens\n    60\t        return attrs\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tasync def measure_context(client, request: dict, compacted: bool) -> ContextMeasure:\n    64\t    try:\n    65\t        counted = await client.messages.count_tokens(\n    66\t            model=request[\"model\"],\n    67\t            system=request[\"system\"],\n    68\t            messages=request[\"messages\"],\n    69\t            tools=request[\"tools\"],\n    70\t        )\n    71\t        return ContextMeasure(int(counted.input_tokens), \"count_tokens_api\", compacted)\n    72\t    except Exception:  # counting is best effort; finalize() falls back to usage\n    73\t        log.warning(\"token count failed; falling back to usage\", exc_info=True)\n    74\t        return ContextMeasure(tokens=None, method=\"pending_usage\", compacted=compacted)\n     1\t# procurement-agent\n     2\t\n     3\tProcurement agent for Example Corp business units. It reads vendor quotes and\n     4\tinvoices that arrive by email, checks them against department budgets, raises\n     5\tpurchase orders in the ERP, pays matched invoices, and talks to staff and\n     6\tvendors in Slack. It keeps short per-department notes between runs.\n     7\t\n     8\t## Architecture\n     9\t\n    10\t```\n    11\tmail gateway --HMAC--> /ingest/mail --> documents (Postgres, per business unit)\n    12\tstaff (OIDC JWT) ----> /runs --> ProcurementAgent loop (app/loop.py)\n    13\t                                   |-- PolicyGate (app/gate.py) + approvals (Slack buttons)\n    14\t                                   |-- Budget (app/budget.py)\n    15\t                                   |-- audit graph (app/audit.py -> audit_events)\n    16\t                                   |-- tools:\n    17\t                                   |     read_document, extract_line_items -> LineItemExtractor sub-agent\n    18\t                                   |     get_budget, erp_call, create_purchase_order -> ERP MCP via gateway\n    19\t                                   |     pay_invoice -> payments API\n    20\t                                   |     post_slack_message -> Slack (via slack-proxy)\n    21\t                                   |     memory_read, memory_write -> dept_notes\n    22\t```\n    23\t\n    24\t* **Tenancy.** Each run belongs to one business unit, taken from the `bu`\n    25\t  claim of the caller's verified OIDC token. Documents, notes, approvals and\n    26\t  quotas are keyed by business unit.\n    27\t* **Identity.** The agent runs as the `procurement-agent` service account.\n    28\t  Its projected token (10-minute lifetime) is exchanged at the internal STS\n    29\t  for audience-bound tokens for the ERP gateway, payments API and Slack\n    30\t  proxy. User tokens are never forwarded.\n    31\t* **Approvals.** `create_purchase_order`, `pay_invoice` and vendor messages\n    32\t  require an approval from a role listed in `config/policy.yaml`. Approval\n    33\t  requests are posted to `#approvals-<bu>` with the argument summary.\n    34\t* **Budgets.** Per-run step, time, token, cost, tool-rate and sub-agent\n    35\t  limits, plus per-user, per-business-unit and fleet quotas for daily spend\n    36\t  and run starts. See `config/policy.yaml`.\n    37\t* **Audit.** Every run step is a row in `audit_events` linked to its parent\n    38\t  step, with the six identity fields, policy version, approval id and\n    39\t  decision-time context size. The agent's database role can insert audit\n    40\t  rows but not update or delete them.\n    41\t\n    42\t## Context size\n    43\t\n    44\tLogged on every audit row as `context_tokens` and `context_method`:\n    45\t\n    46\t| method | meaning |\n    47\t|---|---|\n    48\t| `count_tokens_api` | exact request counted with the provider's token-count endpoint before the call (includes cached prefix) |\n    49\t| `usage_sum_estimate` | counting failed; `input_tokens + cache_read + cache_creation` from the response |\n    50\t| `unavailable` | neither available; `context_tokens` is NULL, never 0 |\n    51\t\n    52\t`context_compacted` is true when the harness dropped earlier turns before the\n    53\tcall (`app/loop.py:_compact`). Provider-side truncation is not visible.\n    54\t\n    55\t## Operating\n    56\t\n    57\t* **Halt.** Insert or update a row in `control_flags` (`scope = 'fleet'` or\n    58\t  `'tenant:<bu>'`, `halted = true`) as `procurement_ops`. New runs refuse to\n    59\t  start while a halt is set.\n    60\t* **Release.** Merges to `main` build, sign (keyless cosign), and attest the\n    61\t  image (SLSA provenance and CycloneDX SBOM). Kyverno rejects unsigned or\n    62\t  unattested images in `procurement-prod`.\n    63\t* **Network.** Default-deny egress with explicit rules for DNS, the egress\n    64\t  proxy, the Slack proxy, the database, the ERP gateway and the STS.\n    65\t\n    66\t## Tests\n    67\t\n    68\t```bash\n    69\tpip install -e '.[test]'\n    70\tpytest -q\n    71\t```\n.\n..\nci.yaml","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01R3wYaDqzNzdZ4RpCHzD5KK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
